  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 30,
    "summary": "Job is derided by the children of vile and base men—In his afflicted state, he cries to the Lord—Job says that he wept for those in trouble.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "But now they that are younger than I have me in derision, whose fathers I would have disdained to have set with the dogs of my flock.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, whereto might the strength of their hands profit me, in whom old age was perished?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "For want and famine they were solitary; fleeing into the wilderness in former time desolate and waste.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 29
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Who cut up mallows by the bushes, and juniper roots for their meat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "They were driven forth from among men, (they cried after them as after a thief;)",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 38
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "To dwell in the clifts of the valleys, in caves of the earth, and in the rocks.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 41
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Among the bushes they brayed; under the nettles they were gathered together.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "They were children of fools, yea, children of base men: they were viler than the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 9
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And now am I their song, yea, I am their byword.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "Ps. 69:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ps. 69:12.",
            "prettyString": "Psalms 69:12",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "psalms",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 69,
                    "end": 69,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 12,
                        "end": 12
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "They abhor me, they flee far from me, and spare not to spit in my face.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Because he hath loosed my cord, and afflicted me, they have also let loose the bridle before me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "OR God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Upon my right hand rise the youth; they push away my feet, and they raise up against me the ways of their destruction.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          },
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "They mar my path, they set forward my calamity, they have no helper.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "They came upon me as a wide breaking in of waters: in the desolation they rolled themselves upon me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 17
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 50
          },
          {
            "start": 92,
            "end": 100
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Terrors are turned upon me: they pursue my soul as the wind: and my welfare passeth away as a cloud.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And now my soul is poured out upon me; the days of affliction have taken hold upon me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "My bones are pierced in me in the night season: and my sinews take no rest.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "By the great force of my disease is my garment changed: it bindeth me about as the collar of my coat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath cast me into the mire, and I am become like dust and ashes.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "I cry unto thee, and thou dost not hear me: I stand up, and thou regardest me not.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "HEB answer."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:20",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou art become cruel to me: with thy strong hand thou opposest thyself against me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "TG Cruelty."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Cruelty.",
            "prettyString": "TG Cruelty",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Cruelty",
                "entryId": "tg-cruelty",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou liftest me up to the wind; thou causest me to ride upon it, and dissolvest my substance.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 64
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "For I know that thou wilt bring me to death, and to the house appointed for all living.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 37
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Howbeit he will not stretch out his hand to the grave, though they cry in his destruction.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 35
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "Did not I weep for him that was in trouble? was not my soul grieved for the poor?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:25",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "When I looked for good, then evil came unto me: and when I waited for light, there came darkness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Jer. 8:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jer. 8:15.",
            "prettyString": "Jeremiah 8:15",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jeremiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 8,
                    "end": 8,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 15,
                        "end": 15
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:26",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "My bowels boiled, and rested not: the days of affliction prevented me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:27",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "I went mourning without the sun: I stood up, and I cried in the congregation.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:28",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "I am a brother to dragons, and a companion to owls.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 50,
            "text": "HEB ostriches."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:29",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "My skin is black upon me, and my bones are burned with heat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:30",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "My harp also is turned to mourning, and my organ into the voice of them that weep.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "HEB pipe, flute."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 22
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 30:31",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 30,
        "verse": 31
      }
    ]
  },
